  "notes": "SEC-07 / ADR 0011 blocking simulation. Endpoints: main = app.example on address A (stands in for the Cloudflare-fronted domain), ingest = ingest.example on its own address B behind the attestation-token gate, ingest_shared = an ingest name on address A. Blocks run on the client's path (iptables in the client's netns): dns = drop queries for the name, ip = drop TCP to the address, sni = drop TLS connections whose ClientHello carries the name. Partial: it shows which property tells the endpoints apart under each block, not how a real censor behaves (no ECH, no Cloudflare address sharing, no active probing, no real network). time_s on a failure is the client's 5 s timeout, or ~0 where a drop on the client's own OUTPUT chain fails the send at once (EPERM): it is not a censor's timing."
